# LiveOS Frontend Rules

## Project

LiveOS is a frontend application for tracking and managing different aspects of the user's life.

The codebase must stay simple, explicit, and maintainable.

## Mandatory Stack

Use only this stack unless explicitly instructed otherwise:

- React
- Vite
- TypeScript
- Effector
- Atomic Router
- Chakra UI
- Yarn
- Feature-Sliced Design

## Forbidden Technologies

Do not introduce:

- styled-components
- shadcn/ui
- Redux
- MobX
- Zustand
- Recoil
- React Router
- Next.js
- CSS Modules
- SCSS architecture
- Tailwind CSS
- npm
- pnpm
- bun

## General Principles

- Prefer readable code over clever code.
- Prefer explicit implementation over hidden magic.
- Do not create abstractions before they are needed.
- Do not generate future-proof infrastructure without a real use case.
- Do not duplicate existing logic, entities, features, or components.
- Do not make architectural decisions without explicit instruction.
- Generate only what was requested.

## TypeScript

- Use TypeScript.
- Avoid `any`.
- If `any` is temporarily unavoidable, add a TODO comment explaining why.
- Prefer explicit domain types.
- Prefer `interface` for domain models.
- Prefer `type` for utility types, unions, and mapped types.

## Code Quality

- One file should have one main responsibility.
- Keep files small and focused.
- Avoid files larger than 300 lines.
- Avoid deeply nested JSX.
- Keep business logic out of React components.
- Keep UI components presentation-focused.
- Reuse existing code before creating new code.
